Replace Requirement 3
Old Req 3 is too compressed. Replace it with:
3. The component treats appended samples as one continuous stream. The first sample after construction or clear() is sample index 0, the next is sample index 1, and so on. appendSamples(samples) appends all provided samples as one atomic operation and copies the input array before returning. Each input value is sanitized before storage: NaN, positive infinity, and negative infinity become 0f; finite values below -1f become -1f; finite values above 1f become 1f; all other finite values are stored unchanged.
3. Replace Requirement 9
Old Req 9 only pinned endpoints. Replace it with:
9. Energy is drawn using this exact ARGB color formula after clamping energy to [0f, 1f]:

alpha = 255
red   = roundToInt(255f * energy)
green = roundToInt(152f * energy)
blue  = 0

Therefore energy 0f is #FF000000 and energy 1f is #FFFF9800. Band 0 is drawn at the bottom; bandCount - 1 is drawn at the top.
4. Replace Requirement 10
Make scheduling public-API-driven, not helper-driven:
10. ProgressiveSpectrogram must not block waiting for analysis. When composed with a positive pixel size, it must schedule missing visible columns for the current viewport. Recomposition, redraw, size change, or state revision changes may trigger scheduling, but duplicate pending jobs for the same column and generation are forbidden.
5. Replace Requirement 14
Because renderSnapshot now updates LRU metadata, it cannot say “does not mutate state” absolutely.
Use:
14. renderSnapshot(width, height) requires positive dimensions and renders into a new Bitmap from one immutable snapshot of committed columns and viewport values. It must not call a composable, must not wait for workers or the main thread, must not schedule jobs, must not commit results, and must not change samples, config, viewport, generation, pending columns, committed columns, or Compose revision. It may update LRU metadata for committed columns read by the snapshot.
6. Add these extra requirements
Add these as new subrequirements:
5a. Column and pixel ranges use half-open interval intersection. Two ranges intersect only if rangeA.start < rangeB.end and rangeA.end > rangeB.start. Boundary-touching ranges do not intersect.
10a. Scheduling must be driven only by ProgressiveSpectrogram being composed at a positive pixel size. Tests must not call private or internal scheduling helpers. Recomposition, redraw, size change, or state revision changes may trigger scheduling, but duplicate pending jobs for the same column and generation are forbidden.
11a. Viewport changes do not invalidate committed or pending columns, because columns are defined in sample time, not screen space. A pending column may still commit after a viewport change if its generation and config are current. Eviction after that commit must use the latest visible-column set, not the visible set from when the job was scheduled.
13a. If a committed column is read by renderSnapshot or by the composable renderer, it becomes recently used for LRU purposes. Merely being pending does not update LRU.
14a. renderSnapshot must use the exact same rendering rules as the composable renderer, including half-open range intersection, max aggregation, band orientation, and color formula.
