2. Sample copy, sanitization, partial windows, duplicate scheduling, and color formula
With windowSize = 4 and hopSize = 2, append 3 samples and verify no column is pending or committed. Append enough for 10 samples using values below -1f, above 1f, NaN, positive infinity, and negative infinity; mutate the source array after append. Compose repeatedly at a viewport covering [0, 8). Verify only columns 0, 1, 2, and 3 are scheduled once, rendered energies reflect copied sanitized values, and intermediate energy colors follow the exact ARGB formula.
